<http://example.org/sen0414-ch2125corr-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 21 to 25 corrections"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.3.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch2125corr-lineage/1.3.0> ;
    owl:priorVersion <http://example.org/sen0414-ch2125corr-lineage/1.2.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch2125corr_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.3.0 (2026-11-26): Objective stage only (one stage per version). Each goal is measured by objectives (27 in all), each metric derived from its goal, each with a counted, derived or judged measurement and a query that reads it, a baseline measured on 2026-11-26 (logs gap_measure.log, gap_measure_pages.log and material_ch*.log in 08-tooling/lineage14-opening/) and a baseline observation. Objectives whose figure is met by absence carry the direction Hold. Lessons of Lineage13 taken: no target is a count of something that can be miscounted (the balloon objective counts the examples that lack balloons, 42 today, down to 0; an objective that cannot be read yet says so in its query); the rdodi objective counts existing files modified or deleted; the allowed folders of the outside-files objective are listed in its query; the judged content objective names the recorded-paragraph case Lineage13 counted. CORRECTION OF THE MISSION STAGE 1.0.0 (appended, never edited): it said that the slide text holds '>>>' prompts 67, 39, 39, 38 and 45 times; those are occurrences of the three characters, of which 26 per deck are a lone mark shape on every slide and the rest are prompt lines of code (41, 13, 13, 12 and 19). The new objective DeckPrompts counts all of them. The objectives are written by the table script 08-tooling/lineage14-opening/objective_make_v1_0_0.py, the lineage's own script (a BRSF handover is owed with the others)."""@en .

